WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.868
-We're hanging out with the one
and only Drew Barrymore!

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.067
Drew --
Oh, lookit, I love it.

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:08.267
Come on. The greatest.
Come on. The greatest.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:09.400
♪♪

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.834
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:00:10.834 --> 00:00:13.968
Drew, we're a few months
into the new year,

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:15.968
and you told me that
your mantra for this year,

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:21.167
2022, is the Year of Know --
K-N-O-W.

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.300
-That's right -- Year of Know.
-The Year of Know.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.400
What does this mean?
-Like Carson, Kreskin.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.200
-Yeah.
Kreskin, yeah.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.834
-Oh, the best.
-Yeah.

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:32.567
-Last year was
the Year of Less.

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:36.834
-You want less of things.
-Yes, I'm very maximalist,

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:40.167
gluttonous, live in extremes,
big personality --

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:43.033
nuts, you know, a little bit.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.033 --> 00:00:45.534
And -- But a student of life,

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:47.767
always working on myself,
and every day,

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.334
I get a little bit better,
hopefully.

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:51.968
-Yeah.
-And so I thought,

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:55.734
"What if I took this year,
as, you know,

00:00:55.734 --> 00:01:00.734
just trying to be really aware
of everything I'm learning?"

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:04.801
I feel like we're constantly --
I'm constantly one step forward,

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:07.767
a step back.
And I just thought

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.434
if I could have more confidence
in what I know.

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:15.734
And I don't know about you guys,
but my inner dialog is not kind,

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:20.267
and I would never speak or treat
anyone the way I treat myself.

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:23.968
And knowing that,
that's the Year of Know --

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:26.300
knowing things, recognizing it.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.667
Even if you're
going on a date with someone,

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.767
we all kind of hard launch,
and, like,

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:31.901
"What is the future
going to bring?"

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:34.100
Just enjoy things.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:37.734
Don't worry about the future
and the past.

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.667
Everyone says,
"Try to be present,

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:42.067
try to have balance."
I get so irritated

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:45.601
when they talk like that,
but maybe they're right, so...

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:46.901
-That that makes you
more irritated.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.501
-Yes, which is even more
patronizing and annoying.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:51.133
-Gosh, yeah.
-So I'm like,

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:53.167
"Instead of the year
of running around

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:55.300
like the crazy headless chicken,

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.667
what if I try to act
like this year

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:00.133
that everything I learn

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:02.968
is something I can truly keep,
and the knowledge is there,

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:05.334
and just have
a little more faith in myself?"

00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:07.200
-Love this.
This is fantastic.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:08.801
I love that you do that.
I mean, you --

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:10.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:13.033
The one thing -- another great
thing about the show is,

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:15.767
you really just put yourself
out there, and a good example,

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.801
I remember you had the cast
of "Queer Eye" come on...

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:19.167
-Oh, my God.
It changed my life.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.033
-...and do a makeover for you

00:02:21.033 --> 00:02:23.567
and had you do
an actual live date.

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:24.767
-Yes.
-And you filmed it,

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:27.834
and you showed
you going on a live Zoom date.

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:30.567
-Yeah, which I thought the idea
of a Zoom date was, like,

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.868
"How on Earth...?"
I don't know why, but --

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:35.701
I'm so IRL.
You know what I mean?

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.501
-In real life.
Yeah, you're so IRL.

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:39.367
-I'm so IRL that I was like,
"There's no way..."

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:42.634
-"I mean, totally be IRL!"
-"...I will like a Zoom date."

00:02:42.634 --> 00:02:45.167
-"I know!
A 'Zuhm dut.'"

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:47.968
-I -- I -- I -- I tried it.

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:52.100
It turns out it's not as
prophylactic weird as it seems.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.100
I guess we're all
sort of, kind of --

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.634
This is the new normal.
The water's out of the bottle.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:59.100
It's not going back in.
It's dating apps and Zooms,

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.167
and maybe you can look at it
as a positive of a screener

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:04.734
or a time-saver.
I don't know.

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:07.434
I still want to meet someone
the old-fashioned way.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:08.534
-Right?
-I want to --

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:10.067
You know,
I wrote, actually, a paper

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:12.467
that I'm gonna put on my blog
because I love writing

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.567
and I have a blog
and I've written books,

00:03:14.567 --> 00:03:16.300
and sometimes
you just get inspired.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:21.634
And I -- I walked up to a guy
in a park, and I was like,

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:24.567
"Are you single?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:25.634
And...

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:28.801
-Did his brain explode
out of his head?

00:03:28.801 --> 00:03:30.901
-And he was like, "Perhaps,"
and I said,

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.667
"Well, that's not 'no.'"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:35.200
-So...
-"I'll take 'perhaps.'"

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.601
-And then I was like,
"Are you gay?"

00:03:36.601 --> 00:03:39.300
Because I also
always bark up the wrong tree.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.767
And he was like,
"No, I'm not."

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:46.801
And then we got to talking,
and we had such a good laugh

00:03:46.801 --> 00:03:50.434
and such a lovely talk.
And then I was like,

00:03:50.434 --> 00:03:51.767
"Ooh, I think I forgot
to ask you

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:54.801
a very important question.
How old are you?"

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.834
-Oh.
-And he was like, "28,"

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:59.400
and I was like, "Oh, no!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.667
"Oh, no!"
-Oh, come on.

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:03.434
-And I was like,
"I don't mean this rudely.

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:05.934
You look so much older."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:08.234
And he was like,
"It's funny because it's a joke

00:04:08.234 --> 00:04:10.367
amongst my friends.
They all -- We --

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:12.901
It's a joke in my life.
I look much older."

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:14.934
-Yeah.
-And I was like, "You do."

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:17.400
-Yeah.
"We had a great afternoon.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.868
Have a great life, bud."

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:21.234
-And I just said, "Okay.
That was so fun,

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:23.901
and thank you so much."
We had a great conversation.

00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:26.200
And we didn't bother
with the obligatory, like,

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.601
"Let's exchange numbers,"
and I just said, "Great."

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:32.133
I said, "I got to tell you,
I just wanted to do something

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:34.200
that I could make
myself proud today,"

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.968
and he goes, "I'm proud of you."

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:38.534
[ Applause ]
And I was like, "Thanks."

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:40.868
-Fantastic.
"We got to hang out more."

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:46.534
-And we walked away, and it was
the most positive experience.

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:48.367
I want to do it again.

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:50.434
Was it dating apps
that stopped us

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:54.701
from going up to people
and asking them out?

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:56.701
Now we don't have to worry
about public rejection?

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:59.033
We can just hide behind the app?
Forget it. I'm over it.

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:02.234
I want to --
I want to talk to people IRL.

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:04.334 --> 00:05:07.367
-Yes!

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:09.701
One at a time,
let's go through the audience.

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:12.767
Who want -- No.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.767 --> 00:05:13.834
I wanted to see --

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:15.133
Speaking of
doing something again,

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:16.234
you did something on your show.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:17.968
You do a thing called
"Drewth or Dare"

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:20.234
every now and then.
-At the end of every show.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:22.801
Segment seven, on our way out.
-"Drewth or Dare."

00:05:22.801 --> 00:05:24.934
-You did one...
-And I'll do anything.

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:27.200
-...and it made me laugh.
And it was --

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:31.534
Here was the dare -- try to eat
a lemon wedge and not react.

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:32.934
-Yeah.
-Now people have been doing this

00:05:32.934 --> 00:05:34.300
online, it's on TikTok.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.534
It is called the Lemon Challenge
or something.

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:38.934
Let's do it 'cause I want
to start a movement,

00:05:38.934 --> 00:05:42.868
because I was shocked
to find out

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:44.033
how much I suck at this.

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:45.300
-All right,
so just grab a wedge,

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.434
and we'll go for it.
This is the Lemon Challenge.

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:48.000
-And have you ever done it?
-Never.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.667
-Okay.
-I'm gonna try to pretend

00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:50.868
I am fine.
-Okay, great, good.

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:52.100
-Like, big deal -- it's a lemon.
-Let's do this.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:54.100
-Yeah, of course.
Cheers, bud.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.133
Awesome.
-Cheers!

00:05:55.133 --> 00:05:56.667
-Cheers.
Nice to see ya.

00:05:56.667 --> 00:06:00.734
♪♪

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:02.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:09.467
♪♪

00:06:09.467 --> 00:06:10.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:15.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:17.901
It's just sour.
It's just so --

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:19.400
It was good
at the beginning part.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.367
-And by the way,
these are good lemons.

00:06:21.367 --> 00:06:22.968
This is a quality lemon here.

00:06:22.968 --> 00:06:24.634
-It is a decent lemon
right there.

00:06:24.634 --> 00:06:26.467
Just going for it.
Come on, that's a trooper.

00:06:26.467 --> 00:06:29.000
Drew Barrymore, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.534
Go to DrewBarrymore.com
for more info

00:06:31.534 --> 00:06:33.634
on "The Drew Barrymore Show."

